# Native UI — Guardias

**Goal:** Style with NativeWind (Tailwind `className`); use real platform-native controls — not a Material Design 3 / Material You design system (including react-native-paper).

## Preferred stack

### Styling — NativeWind

- Use **[NativeWind](https://www.nativewind.dev/)** for layout, spacing, typography scale, and colors via `className`.
- Prefer utility classes over large `StyleSheet.create` blocks for app chrome and screens.
- Import CSS-enabled primitives from `src/tw` (re-exports `react-native-css/components`) when using `className`.
- Keep Tailwind theme tokens in CSS (`src/global.css` / `@theme`); avoid one-off hardcoded colors when a token exists.
- For setup/troubleshooting, use the Expo agent skill **`expo-tailwind-setup`** (`.agents/skills/expo-tailwind-setup`).

### Controls — platform native

- Use **[`@expo/ui`](https://docs.expo.dev/versions/v54.0.0/sdk/ui/)** when it fits the platform and SDK.
  - **SDK 54:** SwiftUI via `@expo/ui/swift-ui` (requires a development build; not Expo Go). Wrap SwiftUI trees in `Host`.
  - **Android on SDK 54:** Compose/`@expo/ui` Android support is limited — use React Native core components (`View`, `Text`, `TextInput`, `Pressable`, `Switch`, etc.) and system look. Do not fill the gap with Paper/MD3.
  - On later SDKs, prefer Jetpack Compose / universal `@expo/ui` APIs when available.
- Icons: `@expo/vector-icons` or platform-native icon APIs from `@expo/ui` when present. Do not assume Paper / Material Design Icons name strings.

NativeWind and `@expo/ui` complement each other: NativeWind styles layout/chrome; `@expo/ui` / RN primitives provide interactive controls.

## Do not

- Do **not** implement Material Design 3 (MD3 / Material You) as the app design system
- Do **not** use the `material-3` agent skill for Guardias UI
- Do **not** add new `react-native-paper` components or themes (`PaperProvider`, `MD3LightTheme`, etc.)
- Do **not** invent a custom “Material-like” look to approximate MD3

## Migration note

`react-native-paper` may still be in `package.json` until removed. When touching UI, prefer NativeWind + `@expo/ui` / RN primitives rather than extending Paper.
